Recording 2. British scientists are preparing to launch trials of a radical new way

182
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:10,840
to fight cancer, which kills tumors by infecting them with viruses like the common

183
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:17,300
cold. If successful, virus therapy could eventually form a third pillar alongside

184
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:23,680
radiotherapy and chemotherapy in the standard arsenal against cancer, while avoiding

185
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,360
some of the side effects.

186
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:31,360
Leonard Seymour, a professor of gene therapy at Oxford University, will lead the

187
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,920
trials later this year.

188
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:38,280
One of the country's leading geneticists, Professor Seymour has been working with

189
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:43,840
viruses that kill cancer cells directly, while avoiding harm to healthy tissue.

190
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:49,080
In principle, you've got something which could be many times more effective than

191
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:51,060
regular chemotherapy, he said.

192
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:57,380
Preliminary research on mice shows that the viruses work well on tumors resistant to

193
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,740
standard cancer drugs.

194
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:03,600
It's an interesting possibility that they may have an advantage in killing drug

195
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:08,560
resistant tumors, which could be quite different to anything we've had before.

196
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:14,060
Researchers have known for some time that viruses can kill tumor cells, and some

197
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:17,960
aspects of the work have already been published in scientific journals.

198
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:24,140
American scientists have previously injected viruses directly into tumors, but this

199
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:29,120
technique will not work if the cancer is inaccessible or has spread throughout the

200
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:35,700
body. Professor Seymour's innovative solution is to mask the virus from the body's

201
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:41,320
immune system, effectively allowing the viruses to do what chemotherapy drugs do,

202
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:44,620
spread through the blood and reach tumors wherever they are.

203
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:50,560
The big hurdle has always been to find a way to deliver viruses to tumors via the

204
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:55,080
bloodstream, without the body's immune system destroying them on the way.

205
00:19:55,080 --> 00:20:01,240
The therapy would be especially useful for secondary cancers, which sometimes spread

206
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:04,200
around the body after the first tumor appears.

207
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:09,380
There's an awful statistic of patients in the West with malignant cancers.

208
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:15,300
Seventy -five percent of them go on to die from secondary cancers, said Professor

209
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:20,600
Seymour. Several more years of trials will be needed before the therapy can be

210
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,980
considered for use in the NHS.

211
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:28,900
Though the approach will be examined at first for cancers that do not respond to

212
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:30,140
conventional treatments,

213
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:34,980
Professor Seymour hopes that one day it will be applied to all cancers.

